If you want to make some template customization without building a brand new
theme, you should use this directory to store your customized version of an
official template file rather than editing it in place.
Doing this, it won't be lost during the next upgrade.

For example, if you want your own header, copy
"themes/default/template/header.latte" to this directory (or any other
directory under template-extension/) under whatever filename you want, and
edit it as you like.

No PHP editing is needed: go to the "Extend for templates" page in the
admin, pick "header.latte" as the original template your file replaces,
optionally restrict it to a URL keyword or a specific theme, and submit.
Your replacer must keep the .latte extension, or it won't be discovered at
all.

Feel free to ask in the forum for further assistance :
http://piwigo.org/forum
